system-header declaration
--
libc++ (LLVM 18) <functional>: std::function<int(int)> holding a lambda
returns a nondeterministic value, so the first assertion fails.  The
drops: __format's __get_property and __estimated_width
(cpp20_requires_expression_parameter_pack_of_differing_types), and with
--cpp11 also __functional/function.h:272 and 350 (same root cause) and 394
~__value_func (cpp11_static_member_of_recursive_partial_specialization,
through aligned_storage's default alignment, fixed); with --cpp20 also
tuple:469 __tuple_impl's constructor and function.h:272, and verification
then ends in ERROR.  clang++ 18 -stdlib=libc++
accepts this program, and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
